ry fibred in groupoids\n<MATH_0006>. Altering the morphisms in <MATH_0007>\nwhich do not map to the identity morphism on some object does not alter the\ncategories <MATH_0008>. Hence we can violate the existence and uniqueness\nconditions on lifts. One example is the functor from Example\n<REF_0001> when <MATH_0009> is not\nsurjective. Here is another example.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ec0d570058aac129b5e3a4b031c0ce9c3e8549b75f039e21cade5246bdb57a7e", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:003S:paragraph/0005"}, "state": "READY"}, "inventory:categories:003S:paragraph/0006": {"context_hash": "sha256:241c0cc9b97044b68b85ea0c73480ee48a63db8577bf1cc2aca9ffe904d5976b", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:003S:paragraph/0006", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 254387, "byte_start": 254051, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:75807796896d527b61e1d12cc6ddef4e691921a58c95ac6f04b326e99b4f561e", "line_end": 7199, "line_start": 7194}, "owner_tag": "003S", "parent_tag": "003S", "semantic_path": "paragraph/0006", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "003S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:320ce68e811ecc861e26ed7a288fb837473bf188b300e34947d264558d943366", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:db76d02ecc1f1d70a890c83a008ab84c7e8b17ec67dff98c935e598b36ae4c57", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLater we would like to make assertions such as ``any category fibred in\ngroupoids over <MATH_0001> is equivalent to a split one'', or\n``any category fibred in groupoids whose fibre categories are setlike\nis equivalent to a category fibred in sets''. The notion of equivalence\ndepends on the <MATH